# Stage a character WITH the Blind-Fight feat attacking an UNSEEN victim, so
# the vicUnseen miss roll at src/Fight.cpp runs over and over (bd inc-4k2).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_BLINDFIGHT_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/blind-fight-miss.keys <seed>
#
# Read the result with tools/check_blind_fight_miss.sh, which builds a scratch
# module holding the test god, runs this script over many seeds and tallies the
# probe's logs/blindfight.log. This file only produces the session.
#
# THE ORACLE IS THE GAME'S OWN HELP. The Combat Options "Avert Eyes" row
# (src/Player.cpp:996-997) states the rule this check tests: averting the eyes
# "gives you a 50% miss chance in combat (25% if you have the Blind Fighting
# feat)". The defect is that the miss roll asks HasStati(FT_BLIND_FIGHT) -- a
# status lookup by number -- instead of HasFeat, and FT_BLIND_FIGHT == CHARGING
# == 75, so an attacker who simply is not charging never gets the 25%.
#
# THE ATTACKER'S FEAT is granted deterministically by "Blind Fight Test God"
# (tools/fixtures/blind-fight-god.irh), spliced onto a scratch module by the
# check, so it does not depend on what the seed offers at character generation.
#
# THE VICTIM is a poltergeist (lib/mon3.irh:3998): SZ_MEDIUM, naturally
# invisible (INV_IMPROVED), 3 HD. The attacker cannot perceive it, so
# e.vicUnseen is true and the miss block runs. Freeze Monsters keeps it from
# taking a turn, retaliating, or chasing the player away, while leaving it
# attackable. The "Attack" verb in the Combat Options menu (src/Player.cpp:880)
# exists exactly for a target that is "invisible or otherwise imperceptible",
# so the attacker can strike what it cannot see.
#
# CHEAT DEATH and INFINITE MANA are enabled together with Freeze Monsters in
# one visit to the wizard switch list (rows 0, 7 and 10).
#
# 20 attack repetitions give roughly 20 unseen attacks per session; the check
# sums them over seeds and asserts on at least 100.

@include sneak-invis-chargen.keys

SPACE   # dismiss the arrival-room description

# Wizard switches: Cheat Death (row 0), Infinite Mana (row 7), Freeze
# Monsters (row 10).
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*7
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
ESC

# Grant the attacker FT_BLIND_FIGHT deterministically.
w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Blind Fight Test God" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

# Summon a naturally invisible victim one square east.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Spirits"
@choose "poltergeist"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:victim

# The measured attacks: the Combat Options "Attack" verb at the unseen victim.
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
c
@choose "Attack"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:end

@quit
